@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Drop maps here
+
+Put Tiled **`.tmx`** map files in this folder, then run:
+
+```bash
+cd server
+deno task import-maps
+```
+
+They'll be parsed, validated, and added to the pool the AI picks from.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- **Format must be `.tmx`** (Tiled). The ROM build runs maps through
+  `tmx2ea`, which only reads Tiled files. If you have `.map`, `.mar`, or
+  `.fmp` files, open them in [Tiled](https://www.mapeditor.org/) and save
+  as `.tmx` first.
+- **The tileset must be named with its 8 hex IDs**, e.g. `3C00CE3E`
+  (ObjectType `3C`, PaletteID `CE`, TileConfig `3E`). This is how the ROM
+  knows which graphics to load.
+- **That tileset's `.png` must exist** in `romBuilder/Maps/Tilesets/`.
+  Maps referencing a missing tileset are rejected, because they'd
+  otherwise build into a chapter with corrupted graphics.
+
+Maps failing any of these are skipped with an explanation; the rest still import.
+
+## Options
+
+| Flag | Effect |
+| --- | --- |
+| `--dir <path>` | Import from a different folder |
+| `--force` | Re-import maps that already exist |
+| `--use-ai` | Describe areas with an OpenAI vision model instead of deriving them from tile data (needs `OPENAI_API_KEY` and a matching `.png`) |
